tasks.description:
Repository: a small ESM JavaScript package (package.json has `"type": "module"` and `"test": "node --test"`; no dependencies). Environment is native Windows; run the tests with `npm test`.

Bug: `overlaps(a, b)` in src/overlaps.js is currently `return a.start <= b.end && b.start <= a.end` (line 3). It ignores an optional `open` property, so intervals that only touch at an excluded end point are reported as overlapping.

Required behaviour: an interval may carry an optional `open: true` property meaning its `end` point is excluded (half-open [start, end)); `start` is always included. Make each comparison strict only when the interval whose `end` takes part in that comparison is open:
- the comparison of `b.start` against `a.end` uses `<` when `a.open` is truthy, otherwise `<=`;
- the comparison of `a.start` against `b.end` uses `<` when `b.open` is truthy, otherwise `<=`.
Intervals without `open` (or with `open: false`) must behave exactly as before. Do not add validation, new exports or helper modules; src/index.js re-exports `overlaps` and needs no change. Update the JSDoc comment on line 1 of src/overlaps.js so it no longer claims the intervals are always closed, keeping it a one-line comment in the same style.

Tests: add regression tests to test/overlaps.test.js, below the two existing tests and in the same one-line style (`test('name', () => assert.equal(overlaps(...), expected))`, importing from '../src/index.js' as the file already does). Do not modify or remove the two existing tests. Cover at least:
- `overlaps({ start: 1, end: 3, open: true }, { start: 3, end: 5 })` is false;
- the same touching case with the arguments swapped, `overlaps({ start: 3, end: 5 }, { start: 1, end: 3, open: true })`, is false;
- `open` on the interval whose end is not the touching point does not change the result: `overlaps({ start: 1, end: 3 }, { start: 3, end: 5, open: true })` is true;
- half-open intervals that share more than an end point still overlap, e.g. `overlaps({ start: 1, end: 4, open: true }, { start: 3, end: 5 })` is true;
- both intervals open and touching, `overlaps({ start: 1, end: 3, open: true }, { start: 3, end: 5, open: true })`, is false.

Run `npm test` and confirm every test passes before finishing.
